{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:3eaba0bbbbea425b","name":"Y-Wing \"LongProbe\"","source":{"id":"source:reference-3eaba0bbbbea425b","title":"Y-Wing \"LongProbe\"","revision":18851,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:51:14Z","sha256":"bf6f166766a58bdfec7bbe5ec4628692e2f39f62b129fe4287c6f3d2574e69bf","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18851","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Y-Wing%20%22LongProbe%22&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-3eaba0bbbbea425b","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebel Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:52c543ff6d31425c"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The \"LongProbe\" variant of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Y-Wing"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Y-Wing"}," is a scouting vessel. It replaces a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," with additional supplies and fuel, a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Navicomputer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Navicomputer","referenceId":"reference:4ae152610571a224"},", a backup ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"},", and a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sensor Enhancement Package"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sensor_Enhancement_Package","referenceId":"reference:b8f9ecb747f86165"},". This is hardly enough to turn it into a dedicated long-range scout, though it can do a better job at that task than a typical ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},". One side effect of this alteration is that \"LongProbes\" are unusually well armed for a scout, making them more likely to get home to report their limited intelligence, and occasionally allowing the \"LongProbe\" pilot to blow up some valuable target uncovered during a scouting mission.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Even so, very few Y-Wing \"LongProbes\" are sent out on their own. Because of their high availability, such jury-rigged scouts are generally sent out in groups of six to twelve fighters, called recon teams. Although a single Y-Wing \"LongProbe\" isn't a particularly effective scout ship, a group of these fighters can scour a fairly large area of space in a reasonable amount of time. \"LongProbe\" pilots actually take great pride in doing good jobs despite their secondhand equipment.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Y-Wing \"LongProbe\" Statistics (CL 10)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +5; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +11\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 16 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 12), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 26; +7 Armor, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicular Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicular_Combat","referenceId":"reference:31246426131b3457"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hi